# Source assets & build helpers — not part of the published site
Source Files/
Website Notes.txt

# The pre-push guard runner moved to the PRIVATE desktop repo (tools/website-sync.ps1) so a
# fresh clone cannot silently lose the four safety checks. This rule stays as a backstop: this
# repo is public and Vercel serves its root, so a stray copy here would be downloadable at
# /sync.ps1. There should be exactly one copy, and it is not this one.
sync.ps1

# Dependencies. Vercel installs these itself from package.json — a local `npm install` here
# must never reach the repo. ⚠ This repo is PUBLIC, and node_modules is thousands of files.
node_modules/

# Secrets. ⚠ This repo is PUBLIC and Vercel serves its root, so a stray env file here would be
# downloadable at /.env — and `vercel env pull` writes exactly that, carrying EVERY project
# secret (MailerLite, Stripe verify, Blob, signup token) in one file. No env file has any
# business in this repo: local tooling reads the gitignored .env in the desktop project root,
# and production reads Vercel's own environment. This rule is the backstop for the one command
# a future session is most likely to reach for.
.env
.env.*

# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.tmp
*~
.vscode/
.idea/

# Python bytecode cache
__pycache__/
*.pyc
